@startuml 05_sequence_login
!include ../style.iuml
title Sequence diagram: sign-in and access control of a request
autonumber
skinparam maxMessageSize 230

actor "User\n(badge)" as U
participant "Browser\nor client" as C
participant "Reviewer\nAPI" as API
participant "Access\nservice" as AS
database "Users\n(MongoDB)" as DB
participant "Security\nlog" as LOG

== Sign-in ==
U -> C : badge, password, one-time code
C -> API : POST /auth/login
API -> API : refuse (429) if this address has too many\nrecent failures (limit per time window)
API -> AS : login(badge, password, code)
AS -> DB : read the user
alt unknown, locked or inactive account
  AS -> AS : dummy password check (same duration)
  AS -> LOG : failure (the real reason is logged)
  AS --> API : refusal
  API --> C : 401, identical answer whatever the cause
else valid account
  AS -> AS : compare the password (bcrypt)
  AS -> AS : verify the code (RFC 6238); a code works once
  alt wrong password or code, or replay store unavailable
    AS -> DB : count the failure; at the 5th, lock the account for 15 minutes
    AS -> LOG : failure (fails closed if the replay store is down)
    AS --> API : refusal
    API --> C : 401, identical answer (503 if the store is unavailable)
  else everything correct
    AS -> AS : create the signed token (jti, expiry)
    AS -> LOG : successful sign-in
    AS --> API : token, CSRF token
    API --> C : httpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict cookie + CSRF token
  end
end

== Protected request ==
C -> API : request + cookie (+ CSRF header if it changes data)
API -> AS : authenticate(token)
AS -> DB : is the token revoked? read the current permissions
alt token missing, expired or revoked
  API --> C : 401
else CSRF header wrong on a state-changing request
  API --> C : 403 csrf
else password change still required
  API --> C : 403 password_change_required
else permission missing
  API -> LOG : forbidden (badge, method, path)
  API --> C : 403
else permission granted
  API -> API : run the action (the actor comes from the session)
  API --> C : 200, answer masked according to the level
end

== Sign-out ==
C -> API : POST /auth/logout
API -> AS : revoke the jti
AS -> DB : record the revocation
API --> C : 200

note right of AS
  Permissions are read again from the database at
  each decision: a demotion takes effect at once and
  nothing is cached.
end note
@enduml
